I've written the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore, so git add refused it and the || true hid the failure. The files are on disk for the implementation phase; I didn't force-add them.

Task 1: Fixes #1174 (product, self-driven slot). A comment after a section header, like [directories] # note, makes yoyo skip the whole section. For the [directories] and [permissions] deny lists, that means the run goes ahead with no restriction. The warning added on Day 255 (#1171) then wrongly says deny is not a key yoyo reads.
• Fix: one shared header reader in config_unknown_keys.rs that all six section parsers call. It strips the comment only outside quotes, and a table of near-miss rows pins its behaviour.
• Tests: end-to-end deny tests through the real parsers, a sabotage check that the test catches the bug, and a probe of the built binary against a dead local port. The existing test that pins the bug as expected behaviour gets flipped and renamed.
• Size gate: config.rs is at its line cap, so the edits replace the check in place and tests go in the other module.

Task 2: Fixes #1176 (product, backlog-drain slot). The "treating unknown provider X as OpenAI-compatible" warning prints 5 times per -p run. The task first lists every place that prints it and which input reaches each (flag, config file, /provider). It then makes the warning print once per process, with a test on the built binary that counts exactly 1 line per run (and 0 for a known provider) and a sabotage check that the test catches the old repetition.

